      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/centenary_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Remnants of Ella's Grove Plantation highlight the area's nineteenth-century reliance on cotton farming and steamboat transport along the Little Pee Dee.",
